## Expected Outcome

The expected outcome of this project is a simple and easy-to-use vehicle rental system that can manage basic rental operations through a terminal interface.

The system should correctly maintain vehicle availability, calculate rental costs, store rental records, process vehicle returns, and calculate total rental income.

## Scope of the Project

This project focuses on basic vehicle rental management and is intended for learning and educational purposes.

The current version manages data during program execution using Python lists. It does not include a database, graphical user interface, online payment system, user authentication, or permanent file-based storage.

## Conclusion

The Vehicle Rental Management System provides a practical way to understand how Python can be used to create a real-world management application.

By developing this project, basic Python concepts such as functions, lists, loops, conditions, input handling, exception handling, and calculations can be applied together in one complete project.